  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two sonometer wires <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;are fixed on a sonometer. The ratio of their lengths, diameters, densities and tensions are given below:</p>\r\r<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>36</mn><mn>35</mn></mfrac></math>;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math>;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math>;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ρ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ρ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p>\r\r<p>If the higher frequency among the two wires is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>360</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>, then what is the beat frequency (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Hz</mi></math>) observed when the two wires are sounded together?</p>\r"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "10",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Frequency of sonometer wire is given by<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#965;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mrow><msup><mi>&#960;r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#965;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>&#960;r</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#965;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>&#960;r</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#965;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#965;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#961;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#965;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#965;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>35</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>35</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></math><br /><br />Since&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#965;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#965;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, this means&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#965;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>360</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p><p>Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#965;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>360</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>35</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>350</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mi>beat</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#965;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#965;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p>"
  }
}